
## AI review loop (ai-review-kit — auto-run)

When CREATING a pull request in this repo, fill every section of
`.github/pull_request_template.md` with real content — actual verification results,
real trade-offs with reasoning. The AI reviewers treat stated trade-offs as intentional
and verify Verification claims; empty or false sections make reviews worse, not softer.

After opening ANY pull request in this repo, immediately and without being asked:
fire the Codex trigger (`gh pr comment <N> --body "@codex review"`) — skip it if an
ack for this head already exists OR the repo has no Codex leg (no `## Code Review
Rules` section in AGENTS.md) — then read `.github/ai-review-loop.md` fully and drive
it to convergence. The trigger is NOT fire-and-forget: the playbook's trigger-timeout
rule owns confirming Codex actually responded. It is autonomous by design — only its critical escalations stop for a
human, and it NEVER merges. Report the end state in one line.

After ANY push to an already-open pull request — inside a loop round or not (amending
a docs PR, a follow-up commit): re-fire the Codex trigger for the new head — skip it if
an ack for this head already exists OR the repo has no Codex leg. Claude re-runs on the
push automatically; Codex runs ONLY on the trigger.

At the START of a session in this repo: `gh search prs --author "@me" --state open
--repo <this repo's owner/name>` — THIS repository only (other repos' sweeps belong to
their own sessions/crons); anything actionable → run the playbook's sweep mode
unprompted, restricted to this repo. Quiet when idle.
(Coverage between sessions is owned by the scheduled babysitter, which runs from the
ai-review-kit CLONE — `<kit>/babysit.sh --install-cron` from this repo's root; the
scripts are deliberately not vendored into the repo. Do NOT also create a Claude
scheduled task for sweeping: it runs under interactive permission settings and doesn't
take the script's lock.)

Installed by ai-review-kit's setup.sh — keep this section when editing CLAUDE.md.
